# Commercial S8.3 direct transport hardening

Date: 2026-08-31  
Scope: offline application and Control SSOT only  
Server contact: none  
Server activation: none

## Finding

The Python standard URL opener used by the S8 Telegram adapter could inherit
ambient HTTP(S) proxy variables and could follow provider redirects. The
dedicated bot credential is embedded in the Telegram Bot API request URL, so
either behavior created an avoidable credential-routing boundary even though
the configured origin itself was exactly allowlisted and TLS verified.

## Remediation

Application PR #82 was reviewed and merged by merge commit
`2e8fdfd305ff8237fe78c8da232e63cbf591ec4b` with tree
`67739e865473bc3e5a9e4dfdd18fbd305c5944b7`.

The canonical client now:

- rejects every HTTP redirect before any credential-bearing follow-up request;
- ignores ambient proxy environment variables for Telegram API traffic;
- preserves the exact `https://api.telegram.org` contract boundary; and
- returns the non-retryable safe code `S8_TELEGRAM_REDIRECT_BLOCKED`.

The application test suite is green at 838/838. Pull-request and post-merge CI
are green on Python 3.10 and 3.13 and PostgreSQL 17.11 and 18.6.

## Control binding

This Control change binds the S8 deployment target to the canonical application
merge above, records that provider redirects and ambient transport proxies are
forbidden, and refreshes the controller digest. No schema, migration, systemd
unit, credential, provider state, server file, service, or public route changes
in this step.

## Runtime decision

The server remains on the previously verified S7 fallback. S8.3 server
reacceptance and its required two-hour observation remain pending until a fresh
authenticated Tailscale session is available. Adult media, identity data, AVS,
payments, publishing, controlled beta, and production stay disabled.
